{"title":"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_by_MathTalks_😉\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by MathTalks 😉</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle(Goes_Through_Full_Thought_Process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle(Goes Through Full Thought Process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution  (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/1250de9d1f8f0b0bd2f59971a5f9ddcdd24017fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(5,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c957ee07fc4636a987ac904325de31f5f7ad9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(11,7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fa95de1d6ad79682782173b35296a5db6285c50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(3,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01fd1949be3a4c80733e61cd9bf5fb28973dc22b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is 12. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1150ef27a4bba82b5f1aa665dc3e1dbe92d9f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw((3,11)--(11,7)--(5,7)--(3,11));  dot((5,7)); label(&quot;$A(5,7)$&quot;,(5,7),S);  dot((11,7)); label(&quot;$B(11,7)$&quot;,(11,7),S);  dot((3,11)); label(&quot;$C(3,y)$&quot;,(3,11),NW);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"132\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc59c95c8cb24d95268445c9c7cc819bb6ae9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }8\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }9\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }11\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the triangle has a base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we can plug in that value as the base. Then, we can solve the equation for the height. Doing so gives us, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e448c160a210aadf166e977d28c622077d4e0ddf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{6h}{2}=3h=12.\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" />\nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/53344018c916a8199658e7f1f4d8b94f1f0b869f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, so that means that we have to add 4 to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9fefb75c3adc05122029adbbdd83d3f26c0892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+4=\\boxed{(D) 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"126\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Shoelace Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e591e2f36b5c02ee96205eecdb5aaff7ca3d8450.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}|(y \\cdot 11 + 7 \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot 3) - (3 \\cdot 7 + 11 \\cdot 7 + 5 \\cdot y)| = \\frac{1}{2}|(11y + 56) - (98 + 5y)| = \\frac{1}{2}|6y - 42|.\\]\" width=\"581\" height=\"37\" /> From the problem, this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We now solve for y.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc8bafc32026ff4bf61c4f4e7688f63757f8c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}|6y - 42| = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb86ae94bfd3456bb92f23a284a0e1fdfea499f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|6y-42| = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfb2949aaa248730cf6d8b3bdcf64d98a754c651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6y - 42 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" /> OR <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a60cacf8cf750eb4864b77cbb403949a7a87a245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6y - 42 = -24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da9ace4a9af5738040df87ec89473060af24eecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6y = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> OR <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de92ddd91e3614e8c0f9f5086e80351f51256a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6y = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c832e4ebb5fc13830ee1f7897c5ac56e83f94e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> OR <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6389a3877e2c9d09826aa0c5e5aa564d8c355afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>However, since, as stated in the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6af927f8045f5d49afae45410f930f399c1b17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, our only valid solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/3869d5c8fa9d0c7f3d6d25054eb5c8b6df8a4c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cxsmi\">cxsmi</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in the figure, the triangle is determined by the vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/907bb24096faed5fe16e7a41de6cb4f27f69b131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ y-7\\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"61\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea03d8aae1e675baab93d799c883185e0939dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{bmatrix}6\\\\0\\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"30\" height=\"45\" />. Recall that the absolute value of the determinant of these vectors is the area of the parallelogram determined by those vectors; the triangle has half the area of that parallelogram. Then we must have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e667f09c25ed80e3310dddb8e0293fc1f09515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}|\\begin{vmatrix}-2 &amp; y-7\\\\6 &amp; 0\\end{vmatrix}| = 12 \\implies \\begin{vmatrix}-2 &amp; y-7\\\\6 &amp; 0\\end{vmatrix} = \\pm 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"365\" height=\"45\" />. Expanding the determinants, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee73042e0b609cb16e0467e7b927d3ab6da1cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6(y-7) = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/2/43200d24d2afab049ae652d036d5afe32ac75132.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6(y-7) = -24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />. Solving each equation individually, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6389a3877e2c9d09826aa0c5e5aa564d8c355afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c832e4ebb5fc13830ee1f7897c5ac56e83f94e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. However, the problem states that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c6af927f8045f5d49afae45410f930f399c1b17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, so the only valid solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/3869d5c8fa9d0c7f3d6d25054eb5c8b6df8a4c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cxsmi\">cxsmi</a> (again!)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Draw a rectangle so that the hypotenuse is the diagonal of the rectangle. The base is 8 and the height is \\( y - 7 \\), so the area is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a042f4456cd9fe932af3d5ea34be37b6e242578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${8(y - 7) = 8y - 56}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Inside the rectangle, there are 2 extra right triangles along with the original triangle. The larger right triangle has an area of half the rectangle, so it has an area of\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41dcb932a753800307a4708bd5945c37f959bba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{8y - 56}{2} = 4y - 28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The smaller right triangle has a base of 2 and a height of \\( y - 7 \\), so its area is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4eef440f1cfa6094b6f3a2c4a28e2bbb5cd62d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\frac{2(y - 7)}{2} = y - 7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the extra right triangles from the area of the rectangle, you get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/319fdd444f08443b2402b962580a3a6a0093c927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(8y - 56) - (4y - 28) - (y - 7) = 3y - 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"331\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since the problem told us that the original triangle had an area of 12, you get the equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05bf3915f6d0e5e913eee4423b933ce194033865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3y - 21 = 12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253acd93d8a68cac8ec1dde0c9d0703e3969e757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3y = 33}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/571a0a3c229eea2720dd573cb85f22e10429d967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${y = 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>So the answer to the problem is \\( \\boxed{\\textbf{D}} \\).\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then the base times height must be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can see that the base is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, subtracting the smaller x value from the larger x value of the two coordinates. So the change of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> value from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />'s y value gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>- mathdragonmochi \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8GHuS5HEoWc\">https://youtu.be/8GHuS5HEoWc</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oMYs2Gg0ays\">https://youtu.be/oMYs2Gg0ays</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"E